ity scans while preserving admission records[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Complete sase-1sl.1 with a metadata-light capacity scanner, a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]persistent never-live cache, and measured parity and scan-cost [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]evidence.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]capacity_scan_core.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/capacity_scan_tui_runaway.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Classify capacity candidates before constructing full records[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capacity-projection[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity-projection: in linked sase-core, implement the marker precheck [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and compact metadata classification for both capacity scan entry points;[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preserve retention closure and pre-retention clan context, remove [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repeated archive-wide clan-member cloning, and add an independent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy-path parity oracle.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Persist validated never-live classifications across processes[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capacity-verdict-cache[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capacity-projection[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity-verdict-cache: persist the compact classification and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]closure/context keys for safely cacheable never-live candidates, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invalidate changed metadata and directories, keep live-marker and PID [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]uncertainty conservative, and prove corrupt-cache, concurrent-writer, [/#D7D7AF]\n   